    {
      "stem": "What is Mean Squared Error (MSE) in regression, and how does it measure the difference between predicted and actual numerical values?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Definition",
      "answer": "b",
      "options": [
        "Mean Squared Error is the average absolute distance between predicted and true numerical values. It removes signs from each mistake without squaring, giving an error score in the original target units.",
        "Mean Squared Error is the average squared distance between predictions and actual numerical values. Calculate each prediction error, square it, then average the squared values to measure overall regression error.",
        "Mean Squared Error is the squared average signed difference between predicted and actual numerical values. It first allows positive and negative mistakes to cancel, then squares their remaining mean.",
        "Mean Squared Error is the square root of the average squared distance between predicted and actual numerical values. Its value stays in the target's original units, making typical mistakes directly interpretable."
      ],
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Mean Squared Error (MSE) is the average of squared differences between predicted and actual numerical values. Subtract the real value from each prediction, square the error, add the squares, and divide by the number of examples. Lower MSE means smaller squared errors when comparing the same target and evaluation data. Imagine estimating daily bicycle rentals: missing by 10 adds 100 to the squared-error sum, while missing by 2 adds only 4.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"mse-figure\"><span class=\"mse-kicker\">QUESTION 01 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"mse-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"mse-title-1 mse-desc-1\"><title id=\"mse-title-1\">Square the differences, then average</title><desc id=\"mse-desc-1\">Predictions differ from actual values by minus one, plus one and plus two; MSE equals two.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"39\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#278876\">01 · MEAN SQUARED ERROR</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"25\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#2e5368\">Square the differences, then average</text><rect x=\"34\" y=\"113\" width=\"575\" height=\"254\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"840\" fill=\"#537f93\">THREE ACTUAL VALUES AND PREDICTIONS</text><text x=\"61\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"17\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"760\" fill=\"#5b788c\">Case 1</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"189\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"189\" stroke=\"#e4edf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"273\" y1=\"189\" x2=\"237\" y2=\"189\" stroke=\"#e3a077\" stroke-width=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"273\" cy=\"189\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#41a395\"/><circle cx=\"237\" cy=\"189\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#de986a\"/><text x=\"579\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" fill=\"#b27954\">Δ -1</text><text x=\"61\" y=\"263\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"17\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"760\" fill=\"#5b788c\">Case 2</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"257\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"257\" stroke=\"#e4edf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"345\" y1=\"257\" x2=\"381\" y2=\"257\" stroke=\"#e3a077\" stroke-width=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"345\" cy=\"257\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#41a395\"/><circle cx=\"381\" cy=\"257\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#de986a\"/><text x=\"579\" y=\"263\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" fill=\"#b27954\">Δ +1</text><text x=\"61\" y=\"331\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"17\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"760\" fill=\"#5b788c\">Case 3</text><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"325\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"325\" stroke=\"#e4edf0\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"417\" y1=\"325\" x2=\"489\" y2=\"325\" stroke=\"#e3a077\" stroke-width=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"417\" cy=\"325\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#41a395\"/><circle cx=\"489\" cy=\"325\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#de986a\"/><text x=\"579\" y=\"331\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" fill=\"#b27954\">Δ +2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"355\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"680\" fill=\"#618092\">Green = actual    Orange = predicted</text><rect x=\"625\" y=\"114\" width=\"338\" height=\"253\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d5e5e9\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"650\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"17\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" fill=\"#537f92\">SQUARED ERRORS</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"24\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#4b7183\">1² + 1² + 2² = 6</text><line x1=\"652\" y1=\"229\" x2=\"923\" y2=\"229\" stroke=\"#e1e9eb\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"652\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"19\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"710\" fill=\"#4d7180\">Divide by 3 examples</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"327\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"32\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"880\" fill=\"#248f81\">MSE = 2</text></svg></div><p class=\"mse-note\">MSE = sum of squared errors divided by the number of cases.</p></section>"
